From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tty: serial: qcom-geni: power down open ports in system suspend

uart_suspend_port() turns an open port off through qcom_geni_serial_pm(),
which drops the port's runtime PM reference with pm_runtime_put_sync().
During system suspend the PM core holds a runtime PM reference of its
own (device_prepare()), so the runtime suspend never runs and
geni_serial_resources_off() is never called: the SE clocks, the OPP
(CX) vote and the QUP-core and config NoC interconnect votes stay on
through s2idle. On the Retroid Pocket 5 the Bluetooth UART (3000 kBps)
and the gamepad UART (115 kBps) keep the QUP0, CN0 and SN11 BCMs voted
in the RPMh sleep set, and the SoC never reaches CX collapse
(qcom_stats aosd/cxsd stay at 0).

Force the runtime suspend in the late phase, after uart_suspend_port()
has shut the port down, and force the resume in the early phase, before
uart_resume_port() powers the port back on. Consoles keep their own
handling (an ACTIVE_ONLY interconnect tag in qcom_geni_serial_suspend()).

---
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
@@ -2030,6 +2030,35 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/*
+ * uart_suspend_port() releases the port's runtime PM reference
+ * (qcom_geni_serial_pm(OFF)), but the PM core holds one of its own for the
+ * whole system transition, so the runtime suspend never runs: an open port
+ * (a serdev peer such as Bluetooth or a gamepad MCU) keeps its SE clocks, its
+ * OPP vote and its QUP/config NoC interconnect votes through s2idle, and the
+ * SoC can't power-collapse CX. Run the runtime suspend here instead, once
+ * uart_suspend_port() has shut the port down. Consoles keep their own path.
+ */
+static int qcom_geni_serial_suspend_late(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct qcom_geni_serial_port *port = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	if (uart_console(&port->uport))
+		return 0;
+
+	return pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
+}
+
+static int qcom_geni_serial_resume_early(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct qcom_geni_serial_port *port = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	if (uart_console(&port->uport))
+		return 0;
+
+	return pm_runtime_force_resume(dev);
+}
+
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SERIAL_QCOM_GENI_CONSOLE)
 static const struct qcom_geni_device_data qcom_geni_console_data = {
 	.console = true,
@@ -2076,6 +2105,8 @@
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(qcom_geni_serial_runtime_suspend,
 			   qcom_geni_serial_runtime_resume, NULL)
 	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(qcom_geni_serial_suspend, qcom_geni_serial_resume)
+	LATE_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(qcom_geni_serial_suspend_late,
+				 qcom_geni_serial_resume_early)
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id qcom_geni_serial_match_table[] = {
